WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.290
I'm Jenna Fisher, and I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是珍娜·费舍，我是安吉拉·金西。

2
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.150
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

3
00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:13.270
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你打造了终极的《办公室》爱好者播客。

4
00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.790
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

5
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.970
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of VFF stories.
还有幕后花絮以及大量的VFF故事。

6
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.990
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是“办公室女士”6.0版。

7
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.480
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

8
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:27.540
Hello.
你们好。

9
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.160
Lady, we have a great day today.
女士们，我们今天有个很棒的日子。

10
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.680
We have another revisited deep dive episode of Office Ladies.
我们又迎来了一期《办公室女士》的回顾与深度解析节目。

11
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:35.460
Yes.
是的。

12
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.740
Today, we are going to go back over the second half of Season 3.
今天，我们将回顾第三季的后半部分。

13
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.380
We're going to get to your questions, your comments about all the things we missed.
我们将解答你们的问题，回应你们对我们所有遗漏细节的评论。

14
00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.460
We're doing everything from back from vacation to the job.
我们将涵盖从“度假归来”到“求职面试”的所有内容。

15
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.560
Yeah, we are.
是的，没错。

16
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.820
And I want you to know, I'm holding what looks like a small phone book in my hand
我想让你们知道，我手里拿着一本看起来像小型电话簿的东西，

17
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.560
because we went through so many questions and comments,
因为我们收到了太多的问题和评论，

18
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.460
and Jenna and I both jotted a ton down, and we're excited to talk to you guys today.
珍娜和我记了厚厚的一大堆，我们今天很高兴能和大家聊聊。

19
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.480
Yeah, it's like 19, 20 pages, I think.
对，我想大概有19、20页吧。

20
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.780
It is, it is.
确实有，确实有。

21
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.360
But first, we have some exciting news.
但首先，我们有一些激动人心的消息。

22
00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:13.760
We are going to start this off with a deep dive with our awesome cinematographer and director,
我们将通过对我们出色的摄影指导兼导演的深度采访来拉开序幕，

23
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.080
Randall Einhorn.
他就是兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

24
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.040
Randall was the cinematographer for 64 episodes,
兰德尔曾担任64集节目的摄影指导，

25
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.940
and he directed The Accountant's Webisodes, as well as 15 episodes of The Office.
他还执导了《会计师网络剧》以及《办公室》的15集。

26
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.240
This man knows this show inside and out.
这个人对这部剧了如指掌。

27
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.880
We are so excited to talk to him.
我们非常高兴能跟他聊聊。

28
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.180
Guys, Randall was one of our original visionaries for the show.
伙计们，兰德尔是我们节目的最初奠基人之一。

29
00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.980
He really helped shape the world, the mockumentary style.
他真的帮助塑造了这个世界和伪纪录片的风格。

30
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.860
He has also been amazing.
他也一直非常棒。

31
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.520
I've been reaching out to him.
我一直在联系他。

32
00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:42.160
You've been reaching out to him, Angela.
安吉拉，你一直在联系他。

33
00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:47.620
You might remember he gave us all of the amazing details about Michael's car going into the lake.
你们可能还记得，他向我们透露了迈克尔的车冲进湖里的所有精彩细节。

34
00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.180
So, we are really excited to get this deep dive interview with him for the pod.
所以，我们非常高兴能为播客带来这次深度的采访。

35
00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.020
So, you guys, when we all got on the Zoom with Randall, we were so excited to see each other.
各位，当我们和兰德尔一起连线Zoom时，我们见到彼此都兴奋极了。

36
00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:01.660
It was the first time the three of us, I mean, Jenna, I don't even know the last time the three of us were together.
这是我们三个人……珍娜，我甚至记不清我们三个上一次聚在一起是什么时候了。

37
00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.620
So, we got super excited.
所以我们超级兴奋。

38
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.340
We did all of our hellos and forgot to hit record.
我们互相问候完，结果却忘了按录制键。

39
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:08.500
Yes.
是的。

40
00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.800
Sam was like, guys, are you recording?
山姆当时说：‘伙计们，你们在录音吗？’

41
00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.180
And I was like, oh, crap.
然后我说：‘噢，糟糕。’

42
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.160
Yeah.
是啊。

43
00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:15.820
So, when you hear this interview, we're going to jump right in.
所以当你听到这段采访时，我们会直接切入正题。

44
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.260
Because we talked for 20 minutes without hitting record.
因为我们在没按录制的情况下聊了20分钟。

45
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:20.900
Yeah.
对啊。

46
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:21.940
Oh, Sam.
哦，山姆。

47
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.000
Sam, Sam.
山姆，山姆。

48
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.100
Every week, you're like, and should you hit record?
每周你都会说：‘你们该按录制了吧？’

49
00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.080
Every week.
每周都这样。

50
00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.740
Sam, can you play that interview?
山姆，你能放一下那段采访吗？

51
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:39.000
Randall, we always start by asking people basically the same question, which is, how did you come to be on The Office?
兰德尔，我们通常开始时都会问大家一个基本相同的问题，那就是，你是怎么加入《办公室》这部剧的？

52
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:50.180
I was doing a reality TV show, kind of an extreme sports thing, where I had to ski with Sean White and some other legendary skier.
我当时在拍一个真人秀，算是一种极限运动节目，我得跟肖恩·怀特还有其他几个传奇滑雪运动员一起滑雪。

53
00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:55.100
And I had to keep up with these guys skiing and film these extreme skiers in Jackson Hole.
我得紧跟这群滑雪的人，在杰克逊霍尔拍摄这些极限滑雪者。

54
00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.660
It was kind of an extreme sports thing for Ben Silverman.
对本·西尔弗曼来说，这算是某种极限运动项目。

55
00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.420
And Ben, at that time, apparently decided, that's the guy.
然后本在那个时候，显然就决定了，就是这家伙。

56
00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.620
Wait, when he decided this, were you flying down a mountain holding a camera?
等等，当他做出这个决定时，你是在风驰电掣地下山，手里还拿着摄像机吗？

57
00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:06.160
Yeah.
对。

58
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.840
I would say that's the guy, too.
我要是他也觉得就是这家伙。

59
00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:21.200
I would say that's the guy for anything, but it is a curious jump to go from guy filming on skis to filming a quiet, contained office cubicle.
我会觉得干什么都选这家伙，但从一个在滑雪时拍摄的家伙，跨越到拍摄一个安静、封闭的办公室隔间，这确实是个奇怪的转变。

60
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:22.000
Yes.
是的。

61
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.180
I went from outdoor adventure guy to the office guy.
我从户外探险的家伙变成了办公室的家伙。

62
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.760
Ben convinced Greg that that's the guy.
本说服了格雷格说就是这家伙。

63
00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:35.240
I remember Greg and I met at a Starbucks, and Greg said, just meet me at the Starbucks on Santa Monica.
我记得我和格雷格在星巴克碰面，格雷格说，就在圣莫尼卡的星巴克见吧。

64
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:41.860
I was new to Los Angeles, and I went to one of the 50 Starbucks in Los Angeles.
我刚到洛杉矶，然后我就去了洛杉矶那50家星巴克中的一家。

65
00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.540
And I finally got in touch with Greg, and I showed up like an hour late.
最后我终于联系上了格雷格，我到的时候大概迟了一个小时。

66
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.740
And Greg is still sitting there, just waiting for me.
结果格雷格还在那儿坐着，就一直在等我。

67
00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.500
And we had a fantastic meeting, and it was wonderful.
我们开了一个非常棒的会，感觉好极了。

68
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.580
And that's where Greg and I really hit it off.
也就是从那时起，我和格雷格真正意气相投了。

69
00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:57.980
Did you bring Matt Sohn into the picture?
是你把马特·索恩带进这个项目的吗？

70
00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.520
He was the camera operator.
他是摄像师。

71
00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:00.960
Yes.
是的。

72
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.380
Had you worked together before?
你们以前一起工作过吗？

73
00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.100
Yeah, you guys knew each other, right?
对，你们以前就认识对方，对吧？

74
00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:11.100
Matt and I knew each other from the outdoor adventure world, and also from Survivor and Eco Challenge.
我和马特在户外探险界就认识，还在《幸存者》和《生态挑战赛》里共事过。

75
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.720
And we filmed scenes together.
我们一起拍过镜头。

76
00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:19.700
And when you're filming a scene together in kind of this verite style, you know, documentary style,
当你们以这种真实电影风格，你知道的，纪录片风格一起拍摄场景时，

77
00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:26.200
you really ascertain really quickly who's looking out for you and who's doing the compliment of what you're doing.
你很快就能弄清楚谁在照顾你，谁在完美配合你所做的事情。

78
00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:30.480
And that verite dance, Matt and I did really, really well.
而这种真实电影的默契配合，我和马特做得非常非常棒。

79
00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:35.420
I remember just a couple times that we've shot together, and he's like, oh, he gets what I'm doing, and I get what he's doing.
我记得我们一起拍过几次之后，他就觉得，哦，他懂我在做什么，我也懂他在做什么。

80
00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:41.060
And we can look at each other out of, you know, out of the eye that's not behind the camera and communicate.
我们可以用没在相机后面的那只眼睛看着对方进行交流。

81
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:46.620
And I just felt Matt was the best person for me to do that dance with.
我只是觉得马特是我进行这种配合的最佳人选。

82
00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:58.420
Randall, were you so bored to be inside of this cubicle warehouse office space with these fluorescent lights after all you guys had shot?
兰德尔，在拍了那么多户外镜头之后，来到这个装有荧光灯的格子间仓库办公室里，你会觉得很无聊吗？

83
00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.020
No.
不。

84
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:00.260
I mean, we had shot.
我是说，我们拍过。

85
00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.260
We had always shot things that we just reacted to.
我们以前拍的东西总是我们自然反应的结果。

86
00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:04.480
That's what cinema verite is.
这就是真实电影的意义所在。

87
00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.060
You're just reacting.
你只是在做出反应。

88
00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.420
You're just gleaning what's happening around you.
你只是在收集周围发生的事情。

89
00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:15.560
And it was really cool to kind of reverse engineer that and actually have to make it look like you were just getting it.
把这个过程逆向工程，实际上得把它拍得像是你在当场抓拍一样，这真的很酷。

90
00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.520
I never really worked in narrative stuff before.
我以前从来没有真正做过叙事类的内容。

91
00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.880
I'd always done, you know, reality and documentaries.
我一直做的都是，你知道的，真人秀和纪录片。

92
00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:28.180
And it was really cool to make scripted stuff look like a documentary because it took another layer of finesse.
把带剧本的东西拍得像纪录片一样真的很酷，因为这需要更高层面的技巧。

93
00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:33.280
You know, normally you're just sitting there and you're filming what happens, and you're just sitting there on a tripod.
通常情况下，你只是坐在那里拍摄发生的事情，然后就坐在三脚架后面。

94
00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:41.840
Had we been sitting there on dollies or on a tripod, and I just know what everybody's going to say, and I'm just doing pans, yeah, I would have been bored.
如果我们当时坐在滑轨上或三脚架上，而且我知道每个人要说什么，我只负责摇镜头，是的，我肯定会觉得无聊。

95
00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:48.860
But to be able to react and, you know, and play a character.
但能够去反应，而且，你知道的，去扮演一个角色。

96
00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:49.380
You were.
你确实演了。

97
00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:50.760
You were a character.
你确实是个角色。

98
00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:51.500
You were.
你真的是。

99
00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:52.660
Thank you.
谢谢。

100
00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:53.200
Yeah.
对。

101
00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.660
You know what, though?
不过你知道吗？

102
00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.220
I did always think of you guys.
我其实一直都在想你们大家。

103
00:05:56.220 --> 00:06:02.840
I mean, Jenna and I have talked about this because we knew, like, some of the adventures you and Matt had had, you had shared with us on set.
我是说，珍娜和我聊过这个，因为我们知道，比如说，你和马特经历过的一些冒险，你们在片场跟我们分享过。

104
00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:08.780
We always sort of chuckled when we would have a situation like a lit candle on stage.
每当遇到像舞台上点燃的蜡烛这样的情况时，我们总会忍不住暗笑。

105
00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:12.320
And Kelly Cantley, our AD, would be like, safety meeting.
而我们的副导演凯莉·坎特利就会说：安全会议。

106
00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.420
We're going to light a candle.
我们要点支蜡烛了。

107
00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:22.600
And, like, Jenna and I knowing that you had a camera strapped to you, like, going down, like, some, like, boat in a river in Borneo.
而且，珍娜和我一想到你身上绑着摄像机，去过，比如说，婆罗洲河里的一些小船上……

108
00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.020
Like, Randall's like, okay, lit candle.
兰德尔就会觉得：好吧，点燃的蜡烛。

109
00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:25.500
Got it.
明白了。

110
00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.100
Yeah.
是啊。

111
00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:28.220
Yeah.
没错。

112
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.600
Safety meetings over a candle are quite, they're really something.
因为一支蜡烛而开的安全会议，还真是……确实挺有意思的。

113
00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.920
It still gets me to this day.
直到今天我一想起来还是觉得很有感触。

114
00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:39.080
But I think it's all under the name of safety because safety never takes a holiday, so.
但我觉得这一切都是以安全的名义，因为安全永不放假，所以。

115
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.140
That's right.
说得对。

116
00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:41.640
Yeah.
对。

117
00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:49.460
Well, Randall, what were some of the early conversations you had with Greg about the look of the show or preserving the documentary style?
那么，兰德尔，你和格雷格最初就本剧的视觉风格或如何保持纪录片风格有过哪些交流？

118
00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.700
Did you guys have sort of a game plan how you were going to shoot and what it was going to look like?
你们当时有没有拟定什么总体计划，比如打算怎么拍，最终呈现会是什么样？

119
00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:54.640
Very much so.
非常有幸有这样的交流。

120
00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.740
I saw the original office, you know, the British version.
我看过原版的《办公室》，也就是英国版。

121
00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.260
And when Greg and I met, I pitched him this idea.
当我和格雷格见面时，我向他提出了这个想法。

122
00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.340
I said it's kind of like a tofu hot dog.
我说这有点像素食热狗。

123
00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:10.420
So it's like good food that's wrapped like bad food.
就像是用垃圾食品的外包装包着优质的食物。

124
00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:19.080
And it's kind of you're putting this fake veneer on it so that people kind of lean in.
就好像你在它外面加了一层假象的外衣，好让人们忍不住凑近去一探究竟。

125
00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:30.380
And the one thing that we always did on shows like Survivor and all reality that I ever did in documentaries is when a conversation is intimate, you back away from it.
而且我们在做《幸存者》以及我做过的所有真人秀和纪录片时，一直都在坚持的一点就是：当谈话变得亲密时，你要退后。

126
00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.220
You don't go to it like normal TV.
你不会像普通电视那样贴上去。

127
00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:40.420
You back away and you back away and you back away because that makes the viewer think that they're privy to something that they shouldn't necessarily be privy to.
你会不断地退后，退后，再退后，因为这会让观众觉得他们窥探到了某种本不该他们窥探的东西。

128
00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:42.900
So they feel in on the joke.
所以他们会觉得自己懂这个梗。

129
00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.480
They feel in on the moment.
他们会觉得自己融入了那个时刻。

130
00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:48.880
And I think it adds a level of intimacy that is really nice.
我觉得这增加了一种非常美妙的亲密感。

131
00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:54.100
As an actor, Randall, I loved how you would back that camera off for those intimate moments,
作为一名演员，兰德尔，我太喜欢你在那些私密时刻把摄像机拉开的做法了，

