1013
00:50:37.360 --> 00:50:37.680
stage.
外面投篮。

1014
00:50:37.900 --> 00:50:39.580
We were like, we have arrived.
当时我们觉得，我们成功了。

1015
00:50:39.940 --> 00:50:42.200
This is going to be the best day ever.
这将是史上最棒的一天。

1016
00:50:42.440 --> 00:50:42.820
Woo hoo.
呜呼。

1017
00:50:43.440 --> 00:50:44.320
12 hours later.
12小时后。

1018
00:50:44.320 --> 00:50:46.220
Did you cry as you left?
你离开的时候哭了吗？

1019
00:50:46.700 --> 00:50:52.520
The difference of us walking to the gig and walking from the gig at the end of the day,
我们去上班时走路和一天结束时下班走路的状态截然不同，

1020
00:50:52.740 --> 00:50:54.160
we were so beaten down.
我们累得精疲力竭。

1021
00:50:54.400 --> 00:50:59.860
I want to say at a certain point, they felt like they weren't getting on camera enough
我想说在某个时候，他们觉得镜头给得还不够

1022
00:50:59.860 --> 00:51:03.600
water splashing on us to indicate that it was a water ride.
有水泼在我们身上，表明这是一个水上游乐项目。

1023
00:51:03.820 --> 00:51:03.980
No.
没有。

1024
00:51:04.160 --> 00:51:08.920
So the first thing they did was they had guys with buckets of water that they would just
所以他们做的第一件事就是找人提着水桶，

1025
00:51:08.920 --> 00:51:12.160
throw on us as we scooted by in the little boat.
在我们坐着小船滑过时直接泼在我们身上。

1026
00:51:12.400 --> 00:51:12.940
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1027
00:51:12.940 --> 00:51:16.020
But at one point, not even that was enough.
但有一刻，连这都不够了。

1028
00:51:16.280 --> 00:51:18.860
They got out what's called a water cannon.
他们搬出了所谓的清水炮。

1029
00:51:19.460 --> 00:51:19.740
No.
不会吧。

1030
00:51:20.340 --> 00:51:20.480
Yep.
没错。

1031
00:51:20.640 --> 00:51:21.320
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1032
00:51:21.520 --> 00:51:24.400
They shoot cannonballs of water at you.
他们向你发射水弹。

1033
00:51:25.240 --> 00:51:29.600
Just drive back to Missouri after that.
经历那个之后直接开车回密苏里算了。

1034
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:32.880
It's like, this is being an actor.
这就叫当演员。

1035
00:51:33.440 --> 00:51:33.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1036
00:51:33.940 --> 00:51:34.880
12 hours.
12个小时。

1037
00:51:35.080 --> 00:51:38.480
I rode that ride one time and I was like, I'm never doing it again.
我坐过那次过山车一次，当时就想，我再也不坐了。

1038
00:51:38.480 --> 00:51:43.480
Well, if you see the commercial, there is a spot where you can pause.
好吧，如果你看广告的话，有一个地方你可以暂停。

1039
00:51:43.660 --> 00:51:47.600
And for one second, half of me is on screen.
有一秒钟，我的一半身体出现在屏幕上。

1040
00:51:48.440 --> 00:51:53.840
So, lady, while you were dancing to this Clay Walker music video, I was getting hit by a water
所以，女士们，当你们在跟着克雷·沃克的音乐录影带跳舞时，我正在挨水

1041
00:51:53.840 --> 00:51:54.240
cannon.
炮轰。

1042
00:51:54.720 --> 00:51:56.000
That's showbiz, folks.
这就是娱乐圈，各位。

1043
00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:57.660
Oh, man.
天哪。

1044
00:51:57.980 --> 00:52:01.600
Well, let's take a break and we will come back and we'll start with business school.
好了，我们休息一下，回来后从商学院开始。

1045
00:52:01.880 --> 00:52:12.040
All right.
好的。

1046
00:52:12.040 --> 00:52:13.280
We are back.
我们回来了。

1047
00:52:13.280 --> 00:52:14.920
We're going to start with business school.
我们要从商学院开始。

1048
00:52:15.180 --> 00:52:17.080
This is the episode with Pam's art show.
这一集是关于帕姆的艺术展。

1049
00:52:17.220 --> 00:52:23.800
And we got mail, lady, from so many artists after this episode because they really connected
女士，这一集播出后我们收到了许多艺术家发来的邮件，因为他们真的对帕姆

1050
00:52:23.800 --> 00:52:24.300
with Pam.
感同身受。

1051
00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:28.160
This is also the episode with the bat in the office.
这也是办公室里出现过蝙蝠的那集。

1052
00:52:28.440 --> 00:52:32.980
And several people shared with us about having bats in their offices.
有好几个人跟我们分享了他们办公室也有过蝙蝠的经历。

1053
00:52:33.240 --> 00:52:33.520
What?
什么？

1054
00:52:33.880 --> 00:52:35.420
Bats in their offices?
他们办公室有蝙蝠？

1055
00:52:35.980 --> 00:52:36.260
Yes.
是的。

1056
00:52:36.420 --> 00:52:37.440
Listen to this one.
听听这一条。

1057
00:52:37.860 --> 00:52:43.420
Kelly Rarden said, rewatching this episode gave me flashbacks of the time I was working
凯莉·拉登说，重看这一集让我想起了我曾在雷雨交加的深夜独自在办公室加班，

1058
00:52:43.420 --> 00:52:50.360
alone in my office late at night during a thunderstorm and a bat started swooping at my head.
结果一只蝙蝠开始朝我的头俯冲过来的那段经历。

1059
00:52:50.520 --> 00:52:56.080
I was on a tight deadline, so I had to dodge the bat for an hour while I tried to continue
当时我正赶着截止日期，所以我不得不一边躲避蝙蝠一个小时，

1060
00:52:56.080 --> 00:52:56.600
working.
一边试图继续工作。

1061
00:52:57.060 --> 00:52:58.920
Kelly, did you get a rabies shot?
凯莉，你打狂犬疫苗了吗？

1062
00:52:59.280 --> 00:53:00.760
I hope Kelly got a rabies shot.
我希望凯莉打了狂犬疫苗。

1063
00:53:00.860 --> 00:53:03.460
Remember, you can't always feel it when they bite you.
记住，它们咬你的时候你并不一定能感觉到。

1064
00:53:03.640 --> 00:53:05.180
I know they're sneaky.
我知道它们可太阴险了。

1065
00:53:05.420 --> 00:53:10.760
And speaking of bats, Kendra Zane said, I can't believe you guys didn't touch on the
说到蝙蝠，肯德拉·赞恩说，我真不敢相信你们居然没提到梅莉迪丝那段暗示狂犬病的伏笔。

1066
00:53:10.760 --> 00:53:12.720
rabies foreshadowing with Meredith.
肯德拉，我们确实应该提的。

1067
00:53:13.000 --> 00:53:14.620
Kendra, we totally should have.
真是个绝佳的发现。

1068
00:53:14.940 --> 00:53:15.640
Great catch.
好了，安吉拉。

1069
00:53:15.900 --> 00:53:16.620
All right, Angela.
还记得鸡尾酒会那一集吗？

1070
00:53:16.800 --> 00:53:17.820
Remember cocktails?
当然记得。

1071
00:53:18.420 --> 00:53:19.140
Yes, I do.
迈克尔去参加了大卫·华莱士家的派对。

1072
00:53:19.420 --> 00:53:21.880
Michael goes to the party at David Wallace's house.
你还记得迈克尔面对镜头采访时，背景里那个诡异的幽灵女士吗？

1073
00:53:22.180 --> 00:53:25.660
Do you remember the creepy ghost lady in the background of Michael's talking head?
我怎么会忘？

1074
00:53:25.820 --> 00:53:26.680
How could I forget?
太诡异了。

1075
00:53:26.940 --> 00:53:27.500
So creepy.
很多人写信来说，他们觉得那是餐饮服务人员里的某个人。

1076
00:53:27.820 --> 00:53:32.260
A lot of people wrote in to say they think it was someone from the catering staff.
哇。

1077
00:53:32.580 --> 00:53:32.920
Wow.
他们指出那个女人穿着和其他餐饮人员一样的酒红色上衣，

1078
00:53:32.920 --> 00:53:39.480
They noted that the woman is wearing the same burgundy top as the other caterers, and they
他们觉得她可能在切什么东西或者在洗碗，

1079
00:53:39.480 --> 00:53:44.920
think she's chopping something or maybe washing dishes because her shoulders and arms are kind
因为她的肩膀和手臂在稍微动一动。

1080
00:53:44.920 --> 00:53:45.960
of moving a little bit.
你们还真是对这一段反复仔细研究过啊。

1081
00:53:46.120 --> 00:53:50.080
You guys really, really gave this a once over.
我是说，如果你连她的肩膀运动都注意到了，那我可太佩服了。

1082
00:53:50.240 --> 00:53:53.040
I mean, if you're clocking her shoulder movements, I'm impressed.
好吧，曼多说那个采访镜头里的幽灵在第六分三十三秒大卫的妻子放下迈克尔的土豆沙拉时，也出现在了厨房里。

1083
00:53:53.040 --> 00:53:58.380
Well, Mando said the ghost from the talking head is also in the kitchen at six minutes,
莱斯利·希斯说，在十四分零三秒时，你能看到她从迈克尔和简的身后走过。

1084
00:53:58.560 --> 00:54:02.520
33 seconds as David's wife puts down Michael's potato salad.
这比我原以为我们能对这位幽灵女士了解到的信息要多得多。

1085
00:54:02.660 --> 00:54:08.300
And Leslie Heath said you can see her walk behind Michael and Jan at 14 minutes, three seconds.
就是说啊。

1086
00:54:08.660 --> 00:54:12.160
This is so much more than I ever thought we would know about this ghost woman.
哦，确实如此。

1087
00:54:12.640 --> 00:54:13.280
I know.
所以她不是幽灵，而是餐饮服务团队的一员。

1088
00:54:13.280 --> 00:54:14.060
Oh, it's so true.
好啦。

1089
00:54:14.620 --> 00:54:17.700
So not a ghost member of catering staff.
我这里还有几个你们发现的细节。

1090
00:54:17.920 --> 00:54:18.300
Okay.
查理说，我想指出的是，当简向迈克尔出示他们的恋爱合同时，迈克尔说：“我要把它装进相框里。”

1091
00:54:18.540 --> 00:54:20.560
I've got a few more catches for you.
而在后来的那一集《听证会》中，当简试图起诉邓德米夫林时，迈克尔把这份合同作为证据拿了出来，而且它确实在一个黑色的相框里。

1092
00:54:20.780 --> 00:54:26.240
Charlie said, I'd like to point out that when Jan presents Michael with their love contract,
太棒了。

1093
00:54:26.580 --> 00:54:28.560
Michael says, I'm going to frame mine.
这真的很绝，对吧？

1094
00:54:28.700 --> 00:54:33.440
In the later episode, The Deposition, when Jan is attempting to sue Dunder Mifflin,
克里斯·G说，你们没提到这样一个事实：简是自己开车去派对的，

1095
00:54:34.000 --> 00:54:38.160
Michael presents the contract as evidence, and it's in a black frame.
但后来却坐迈克尔的车回了家。

1096
00:54:38.640 --> 00:54:38.880
Nice.
她的车怎么处理了？

1097
00:54:39.500 --> 00:54:41.240
It's so good, isn't it?
这真的是一个很棒的发现。

1098
00:54:41.680 --> 00:54:46.500
And Chris G says, you didn't mention the fact that Jan drove her own car to the party,
我简直不敢相信。

1099
00:54:46.640 --> 00:54:48.900
but then rode home with Michael.
大家都太会找了。

1100
00:54:49.360 --> 00:54:51.260
What happened to her car?
真的太感谢大家的分享了。

1101
00:54:51.460 --> 00:54:52.640
I had wondered about that.
我之前一直在想这件事。

1102
00:54:52.740 --> 00:54:58.100
I have to say, I wondered, did they have to drive back to David Wallace's house and
我得说，我在想，他们是不是得开车回大卫·华莱士家，然后

1103
00:54:58.100 --> 00:54:58.760
pick up her car?
把她的车开回来？

1104
00:54:58.840 --> 00:54:59.740
You know what I think she did?
你知道我觉得她是怎么做的吗？

1105
00:54:59.940 --> 00:55:03.220
I think she sent Michael in a cab the next day to get her car.
我觉得她第二天叫迈克尔坐出租车去把车开回来了。

1106
00:55:03.400 --> 00:55:05.100
I think she drank too much wine.
我觉得她喝了太多的酒。

1107
00:55:05.560 --> 00:55:08.100
Oh, well, that's for sure why Michael drove her.
哦，好吧，迈克尔送她肯定是因为这个。

1108
00:55:08.100 --> 00:55:12.180
But yeah, how she retrieved her car, I bet she made Michael go get it.
不过对啊，说到她怎么取回车的，我敢说肯定是让迈克尔去开的。

1109
00:55:12.340 --> 00:55:14.260
And then I bet Michael made Dwight go get it.
然后我敢说迈克尔又让德怀特去开的。

1110
00:55:15.580 --> 00:55:16.020
Exactly.
没错。

1111
00:55:16.480 --> 00:55:16.920
Exactly.
确实。

1112
00:55:17.460 --> 00:55:22.400
Well, moving on to the negotiation, my pocket soapbox got a lot of mail.
好了，接下来聊聊谈判，我那个关于口袋的随性观点收到了很多邮件。

1113
00:55:22.600 --> 00:55:29.780
In support of my position, one of my favorites came from Melanie Vergara, who said,
为了支持我的观点，我最喜欢的一封来自梅兰妮·维加拉，她说，

1114
00:55:29.780 --> 00:55:36.800
Ladies, I feel so strongly about the symbology of pockets that I refuse to even consider buying
女士们，我对口袋的象征意义深信不疑，以至于我甚至不考虑购买

1115
00:55:36.800 --> 00:55:38.520
a wedding dress without pockets.
没有口袋的婚纱。

1116
00:55:38.520 --> 00:55:41.500
And I found the wedding dress of my dreaMs.
结果我找到了我梦寐以求的婚纱。

1117
00:55:41.500 --> 00:55:42.700
It has pockets.
它有口袋。

1118
00:55:42.980 --> 00:55:44.360
She's going to wear it this year.
她今年就要穿着它结婚了。

1119
00:55:44.480 --> 00:55:47.020
I mean, a wedding dress with pockets is pretty phenomenal.
我的意思是，带口袋的婚纱真的很惊艳。

1120
00:55:47.020 --> 00:55:52.460
Well, Kenny, who is a historian, wrote in and had a correction for us.
好了，肯尼，他是一位历史学家，写信来给我们纠正了一个错误。

1121
00:55:52.600 --> 00:55:59.020
Kenny says, women had pockets throughout history until the 1800s, when for various complicated
肯尼说，女性在历史上一直都有口袋，直到19世纪，由于各种复杂

1122
00:55:59.020 --> 00:56:02.560
and mostly sexist reasons, women lost their pockets.
且大多带有性别歧视的原因，女性才失去了口袋。

1123
00:56:02.780 --> 00:56:05.760
So yes, the lack of pockets is a sexist thing.
所以没错，没有口袋确实是性别歧视造成的。

1124
00:56:05.880 --> 00:56:09.220
But the 400 years ago thing is wrong.
但是“四百年前”这个说法是不对的。

1125
00:56:09.460 --> 00:56:11.040
It's more like 200.
更接近两百年。

1126
00:56:11.040 --> 00:56:15.180
Secondly, she says, corsets were not bad for you.
其次，她说，束腰并不对身体有害。

1127
00:56:15.340 --> 00:56:17.300
In fact, they gave you great back support.
事实上，它们能提供很好的背部支撑。

1128
00:56:17.580 --> 00:56:23.000
The reason corsets hurt people today is because they either haven't broken them in the same way
现在人们穿束腰会觉得痛，要么是因为他们没有像磨合硬皮鞋那样

1129
00:56:23.000 --> 00:56:27.400
you have to break in a stiff material shoe before they're comfortable or because they are
把束腰穿软就觉得舒服了，要么是因为它们

1130
00:56:27.400 --> 00:56:32.920
not fitted properly because people today don't realize the absolute importance of a well-fitted
没有量身定制，因为现在的人们没有意识到合身的束腰

1131
00:56:32.920 --> 00:56:38.680
corset and that she would personally take a corset over a bra any day.
有多么重要，而且她个人宁可穿束腰也绝不穿文胸。

1132
00:56:38.980 --> 00:56:39.460
Wow.
哇。

1133
00:56:39.460 --> 00:56:41.220
It's a lot of information there.
信息量真大啊。

1134
00:56:41.600 --> 00:56:43.580
Kenny, I could not love this letter more.
肯尼，我太喜欢这封信了。

1135
00:56:43.980 --> 00:56:44.760
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1136
00:56:44.920 --> 00:56:49.960
Although I do have to say, having worn many corsets for acting projects over the year,
不过我不得不说，这些年来因为演戏穿过很多次束腰，

1137
00:56:50.080 --> 00:56:51.320
perhaps they were ill-fitted.
也许当时那些束腰都不太合身吧。

1138
00:56:51.680 --> 00:56:52.980
I'm going to go ahead and take a bra.
我还是选文胸吧。

1139
00:56:53.260 --> 00:56:55.000
You're going to take a bra over a corset?
你宁可要文胸也不要束腰？

1140
00:56:55.160 --> 00:56:58.420
I'm going to take a sports bra, if I'm being honeSt.
老实说，我宁可穿运动内衣。

1141
00:56:58.700 --> 00:57:02.280
I don't even want any of the underwire if I can avoid it.
如果能避免的话，我连钢圈都不想要。

1142
00:57:02.500 --> 00:57:05.200
You're going to go uniboob and be fine with it.
你宁可变成连体胸（uniboob）也无所谓吗。

1143
00:57:05.420 --> 00:57:06.100
Here's the thing.
是这样的。

1144
00:57:06.100 --> 00:57:11.340
When I get dressed in the mornings, I like to get dressed as if I might have to break
我每天早上穿衣服的时候，我都喜欢穿成好像随时

1145
00:57:11.340 --> 00:57:14.060
into a full sprint at some point in the day.
准备在一天中某个时刻全速冲刺的样子。

1146
00:57:14.300 --> 00:57:14.740
Okay?
好吗？

1147
00:57:15.080 --> 00:57:16.700
Your panic button is ready.
你的警报随时准备着。

1148
00:57:16.700 --> 00:57:19.040
If you need to run, if you need to haul ass.
如果你需要奔跑，如果你需要火速逃跑。

1149
00:57:19.160 --> 00:57:19.320
Yeah.
对。

1150
00:57:19.460 --> 00:57:20.580
I'm dressed for it.
我已经为此穿好衣服了。

1151
00:57:20.580 --> 00:57:23.300
If there's an apocalyptic event, I'm ready.
如果有末日灾难降临，我已经准备好了。

1152
00:57:23.720 --> 00:57:25.860
Men are naturally dressed this way.
男人们生来就是这样穿的。

1153
00:57:26.220 --> 00:57:31.280
Truly, a man could pretty much break into a sprint pretty easily, right?
真的，男人随时都可以轻松地开始冲刺，对吧？

1154
00:57:31.880 --> 00:57:35.940
Well, I want to survive end of times, a possible mugging.
总之，我想在末日和可能的抢劫中存活下来。

1155
00:57:36.100 --> 00:57:36.800
I don't know.
我不知道。

1156
00:57:36.980 --> 00:57:41.020
So no corsets, no Spanx, no high heels for me.
所以对我来说，没有束腰，没有塑身衣，也没有高跟装。

1157
