01:11:07.460 --> 01:11:11.880
So Meredith hits on Jim to sign her caSt.
所以梅雷迪思勾引吉姆来给她签名石膏。

1456
01:11:12.820 --> 01:11:15.260
Phyllis has Jim on her liSt.
菲利斯把吉姆列入了她的名单。

1457
01:11:15.600 --> 01:11:16.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1458
01:11:16.620 --> 01:11:17.180
Wow.
哇。

1459
01:11:17.680 --> 01:11:18.240
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

1460
01:11:18.240 --> 01:11:19.820
The ladies are going after you, fella.
女士们在追求你呢，伙计。

1461
01:11:20.180 --> 01:11:22.600
More fan mail lady from Krista K.
来自克里斯塔·K的更多粉丝来信。

1462
01:11:22.940 --> 01:11:29.380
She says, I believe it was Jenna that equated walking over lava stones to walking on Lego
她说，我记得好像是珍娜把走过火山石比作踩在乐高

1463
01:11:29.380 --> 01:11:29.880
bricks.
积木上。

1464
01:11:30.120 --> 01:11:35.320
I wanted you guys to know that doing a Lego walk, which is walking endlessly on Lego bricks,
我想让你们知道，走乐高挑战，也就是在乐高积木上无休止地走，

1465
01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:38.900
is actually a thing that happens during Lego fan conventions.
其实是乐高粉丝大会期间会有的活动。

1466
01:11:39.760 --> 01:11:43.800
Krista said she tried it once and failed miserably, but her husband did all right one year.
克里斯塔说她试过一次，结果惨败，但她丈夫有一年表现不错。

1467
01:11:43.800 --> 01:11:53.320
And during last year's Philly Brick Fest, the Guinness World Record was set at 2,737 feet.
在去年费城乐高节期间，吉尼斯世界纪录被刷新为2,737英尺。

1468
01:11:53.880 --> 01:11:55.680
But listen to this.
但听听这个。

1469
01:11:55.820 --> 01:12:02.880
That record was shattered on November 20th, 2020 by someone named LA Beast, who took a video of
这个纪录在2020年11月20日被一个叫LA Beast的人打破了，他录下了一段

1470
01:12:02.880 --> 01:12:08.940
themselves walking 12,750 feet over a bunch of Lego.
自己在一堆乐高上走了12,750英尺的视频。

1471
01:12:09.260 --> 01:12:12.520
And there's a video on YouTube, but she said it's like an hour long.
YouTube上有一个视频，但她说大概有一个小时长。

1472
01:12:12.740 --> 01:12:13.960
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

1473
01:12:14.220 --> 01:12:16.960
Someone walked on Legos for an hour.
有人踩着乐高走了一个小时。

1474
01:12:17.280 --> 01:12:22.940
All I could think of as a parent was, oh my God, who had to pick up all those stinking Legos when it was done?
作为一个家长，我脑子里想的全是，天哪，结束的时候是谁去收拾那些臭气熏天的乐高的？

1475
01:12:23.160 --> 01:12:23.420
Yeah.
对啊。

1476
01:12:23.780 --> 01:12:25.000
That's a lot of Lego pickup.
那得捡多少乐高啊。

1477
01:12:25.280 --> 01:12:26.260
It really is.
确实是。

1478
01:12:26.260 --> 01:12:30.880
Moving us along now to the job, fan catch from Erika Jayne.
我们接下来继续，来自埃里卡·杰恩的工作粉丝来信。

1479
01:12:31.580 --> 01:12:40.020
My thought was that maybe this episode is called The Job, not because of all the people who are vying for the corporate job,
我的想法是，也许这一集叫“工作”，不是因为所有争夺公司职位的人，

1480
01:12:40.220 --> 01:12:42.620
but because of Jan's boob job.
而是因为简的隆胸手术。

1481
01:12:43.740 --> 01:12:47.760
I saw a few people sort of had this idea and it cracked me up.
我看到有好几个人都有这种想法，把我逗乐了。

1482
01:12:47.820 --> 01:12:48.200
I know.
我知道。

1483
01:12:48.520 --> 01:12:50.400
It is a bit of a double entendre.
这有点一语双关的意思。

1484
01:12:50.900 --> 01:12:51.520
Double entendre.
一语双关。

1485
01:12:51.900 --> 01:12:52.160
Yeah.
是的。

1486
01:12:52.340 --> 01:12:55.700
This episode also featured a really great interview with Paul Lieberstein.
这一集还包含了一段非常棒的对保罗·利伯斯坦的采访。

1487
01:12:55.700 --> 01:12:59.400
We got a bunch of mail from people saying how much they loved hearing from him.
我们收到了很多人的信，说他们多么喜欢听他说话。

1488
01:12:59.800 --> 01:13:07.540
And lady, we also had people write in and say that they love our tangents, our soapboxes, our deep dives,
而且，女士，我们还收到来信说，他们喜欢我们的题外话、我们的长篇大论、我们的深入探讨，

1489
01:13:07.540 --> 01:13:14.020
because you apologized, because I think you felt a little self-conscious when you were sharing about the limelight,
因为你道了歉，因为我想你当时分享关于那个焦点——哥特式大教堂里面的俱乐部时，觉得有点不好意思。

1490
01:13:14.520 --> 01:13:16.980
the club inside of the Gothic cathedral.
是的，我讲了很长时间，然后我意识到，天哪，我是不是说太多了？

1491
01:13:17.560 --> 01:13:21.920
Yes, I went on for a long time and then I realized like, oh my gosh, am I talking too much about this?
好吧，这种不好意思的感觉，以及努力不去为不需要道歉的事情道歉，真的引起了大家的共鸣。

1492
01:13:21.920 --> 01:13:30.000
Well, this feeling of being self-conscious and trying not to apologize for things you don't need to apologize for really resonated with people.
很高兴看到我们大家要一起为此努力。

1493
01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:33.700
And I am very happy to see that we are all going to work on this together.
是的，我们会的。

1494
01:13:34.120 --> 01:13:35.280
Yes, we are.
好了，伙计们，差不多就到这里了。

1495
01:13:35.600 --> 01:13:37.980
Well, guys, that pretty much wraps it up.
但在我们离开之前，我们确实收到一个提问，是给我们的音响师萨姆的。

1496
01:13:38.080 --> 01:13:42.080
But before we go, we did get a question for our sound engineer, Sam.
萨拉·瓦卡里想知道，你是威斯康星州哪里人？

1497
01:13:42.720 --> 01:13:46.560
Sarah Vacari would like to know, where are you from in Wisconsin?
哦，我来自威斯康星州的沃特敦。

1498
01:13:46.560 --> 01:13:49.140
Oh, I am from Watertown, Wisconsin.
它在麦迪逊和密尔沃基之间。

1499
01:13:49.180 --> 01:13:51.400
It's halfway between Madison and Milwaukee.
我们的吉祥物是一只小鹅。

1500
01:13:51.560 --> 01:13:52.920
And our mascot was a gosling.
吉祥物是一只小鹅。

1501
01:13:53.080 --> 01:13:55.980
It was a very intimidating baby goose in a sweater.
那是一只穿着毛衣、气势汹汹的小鹅。

1502
01:13:56.500 --> 01:13:59.460
Oh, go baby goose in your little sweater.
哦，穿着小毛衣的小鹅加油。

1503
01:13:59.640 --> 01:14:04.560
Angela's doing some candlesticks as she cheers that cheer for your tiny goose.
安吉拉在做一些烛台动作，她为你的小鹅欢呼喝彩。

1504
01:14:04.720 --> 01:14:05.220
Jazz hands.
爵士手势。

1505
01:14:06.020 --> 01:14:10.200
And speaking of local treasures, I wanted to give a shout out to Christy Adventures.
说到当地的宝藏，我想向克里斯蒂历险记致意。

1506
01:14:10.200 --> 01:14:13.880
She sent us a walking tour guide of Scranton.
她给我们寄来了一份斯克兰顿的步行导游图。

1507
01:14:14.020 --> 01:14:14.920
It's like a whole map.
就像一张完整的地图。

1508
01:14:15.040 --> 01:14:15.940
It's amazing.
太棒了。

1509
01:14:15.960 --> 01:14:17.640
And I've already looked at it a few times.
而且我已经看好几遍了。

1510
01:14:17.760 --> 01:14:20.760
You gave me one and I literally love it.
你给过我一份，我简直爱不释手。

1511
01:14:21.040 --> 01:14:22.700
Yeah, we will use that when we go.
对，我们去的时候会用上的。

1512
01:14:22.960 --> 01:14:24.580
Well, there you have it, guys.
好了，情况就是这样，伙计们。

1513
01:14:24.580 --> 01:14:28.000
We have revisited the second half of season three.
我们重温了第三季的后半部分。

1514
01:14:28.620 --> 01:14:32.000
Thank you to Randall Einhorn for talking with us.
感谢兰德尔·艾因霍恩与我们交谈。

1515
01:14:32.400 --> 01:14:36.360
And thank you to Jackie Debiton for sending in those audio clips.
也感谢杰基·黛比顿寄来这些音频剪辑。

1516
01:14:36.980 --> 01:14:37.380
Yes.
是的。

1517
01:14:37.620 --> 01:14:40.360
And thank you to you all for sending in your questions and comments.
谢谢大家发来问题和评论。

1518
01:14:40.500 --> 01:14:41.280
There were a lot.
数量非常多。

1519
01:14:41.440 --> 01:14:43.040
We tried to get to as many as we could.
我们尽量回答了尽可能多的问题。

1520
01:14:43.100 --> 01:14:44.800
I know we missed some, guys.
我知道我们漏掉了一些，伙计们。

1521
01:14:44.960 --> 01:14:45.800
I know we did.
我知道我们确实漏了。

1522
01:14:45.960 --> 01:14:48.300
But, you know, we'll just keep chipping away at them.
不过，你知道的，我们会继续慢慢解决它们的。

1523
01:14:48.400 --> 01:14:52.260
If you want to send us a question or comments, head over to the Office Ladies pod Instagram.
如果你想给我们发问题或评论，请前往 Office Ladies 的播客 Instagram。

1524
01:14:52.540 --> 01:14:53.920
We check all our comments there.
我们在那里的所有评论都会看。

1525
01:14:54.160 --> 01:14:57.500
And if you go to our website, officeladies.com,
如果你去我们的网站 officeladies.com，

1526
01:14:57.740 --> 01:15:01.140
you can find little folders that correspond to each episode.
你可以找到对应每一集的小文件夹。

1527
01:15:01.480 --> 01:15:05.740
That's where we pull the questions for our regular episodes and for our revisited.
我们在常规节目和重温节目中就是从那里提取问题的。

1528
01:15:06.360 --> 01:15:06.840
Yes.
是的。

1529
01:15:06.980 --> 01:15:11.980
And on Office Ladies pod, if you could put your question or comment to the episode it pertains to,
在 Office Ladies 播客上，如果你能把你的问题或评论发到它所属的那一集，

1530
01:15:12.180 --> 01:15:14.860
that way it has a better chance of making it in.
这样它被选中的几率会更大。

1531
01:15:15.380 --> 01:15:17.520
Wait, wait, guys.
等等，等等，伙计们。

1532
01:15:17.920 --> 01:15:20.620
That sounded like something I would say.
听起来像我会说的话。

1533
01:15:21.380 --> 01:15:23.840
Angela, am I rubbing off on you?
安吉拉，我身上有你的影子了吗？

1534
01:15:24.020 --> 01:15:27.480
You just directed people to an organizational technique.
你刚刚指导大家使用了一种组织技巧。

1535
01:15:28.120 --> 01:15:29.960
I've never been so excited.
我从来没有这么兴奋过。

1536
01:15:31.560 --> 01:15:32.380
Oh, gosh.
哦，天哪。

1537
01:15:32.520 --> 01:15:34.420
I didn't know that would do it for you like that.
我不知道这会让你这么激动。

1538
01:15:34.560 --> 01:15:37.740
I'll throw out some more of my home organization tips, okay?
那我再多分享一些我的居家收纳小贴士，好吗？

1539
01:15:37.880 --> 01:15:38.320
Please.
请务必分享。

1540
01:15:38.880 --> 01:15:39.500
All right, guys.
好了，伙计们。

1541
01:15:39.500 --> 01:15:42.120
We will be back next week with a regular episode.
我们下周将带着常规节目回归。

1542
01:15:42.360 --> 01:15:42.740
Love you.
爱你们。

1543
01:15:42.920 --> 01:15:43.660
Love you, guys.
爱你们，伙计们。

1544
01:15:43.820 --> 01:15:44.240
Take care.
保重。

1545
01:15:44.620 --> 01:15:53.330
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听 Office Ladies。

1546
01:15:53.670 --> 01:15:58.710
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
Office Ladies 是 Odyssey 的节目，由珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金西制作。

